  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Solving Trigonometric Equations Using Sine</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>
Consider the trigonometric equation: \(\sin\theta={@given_value@}\)</p>
<p><strong>(a)</strong> Determine the reference angle \(\alpha\).</p>

<p>[[input:ans0]]</p>
<p>[[validation:ans0]]</p>

<p><strong>(b)</strong> Find all values of
\(\theta\in[0^\circ,360^\circ]\) satisfying the given equation.</p>

<p>First solution:</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]]</p>
<p>[[validation:ans1]]</p>

<p>Second solution:</p>
<p>[[input:ans2]]</p>
<p>[[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p><strong>Instructions:</strong> Give all answers correct to 1 decimal place.</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>

<p>We are given: \(\sin\theta={@given_value@}\)</p>

<p><strong>Step 1: Determine the reference angle.</strong></p>

<p>Take the inverse sine of the absolute value:</p>

\(\alpha=\sin^{-1}(|{@given_value@}|)\)

\(\alpha={@alpha_exact@}^\circ\)

<p>Correct to 1 decimal place:</p>

\(\boxed{\alpha={@ta0@}^\circ}\)

<p><strong>Step 2: Identify the quadrants.</strong></p>

<p>Since sine is negative, the solutions lie in quadrants III and IV.</p>

<p><strong>Step 3: Determine the first solution.</strong></p>

<p>In quadrant III:</p>

\(\theta_1=180^\circ+\alpha\)

\(\boxed{\theta_1={@ta1@}^\circ}\)

<p><strong>Step 4: Determine the second solution.</strong></p>

<p>In quadrant IV:</p>

\(\theta_2=360^\circ-\alpha\)

\(\boxed{\theta_2={@ta2@}^\circ}\)

<p><strong>Final Answer:</strong></p>

\(\boxed{\theta={@ta1@}^\circ,\quad{@ta2@}^\circ}\)]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
